      "message": "It looks like aosp/4312484 already covers this. `vma_can_userfault()` returns false for a non-anonymous VMA of a 4KB mm, so the check a few lines below already fails the registration for the same VMAs, including a range that mixes anonymous and file VMAs, before any VMA is changed. It also logs the refusal with `p3s_4k_unsupported()`.\n\nSo as far as I can see, this hunk only turns `-EINVAL` into `-EOPNOTSUPP` and skips the log. `-EINVAL` is also what upstream returns for the other VMAs it can\u0027t register, such as a regular file mapping.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this patch, and have `userfaultfd_shmem_ppps.c` in aosp/4367986 expect `EINVAL`?",
